# exp-ops/configs/core-hrrn-tier-q4.env — GSCH-CORE, Q=4, CPU OFFLOAD ON, the TIER-AWARE
# queue module (`entryOrder: hrrn-tier`). PREREG-multipod-offload §"THE OFFLOAD SOLUTION".
#
# THIS FILE IS core-f5p-q4-offload.env WITH ONE SETTING CHANGED — the entry order. The two
# are therefore a same-build, same-digest, same-deployment pair, and any difference between
# the arms IS the tier-aware order:
#
#     diff docs/gsch-core/core-f5p-q4-offload.env docs/gsch-core/core-hrrn-tier-q4.env
#
# The rule: F5′ EXACTLY (newcomer class as the OUTER key, bounded HRRN inside a class, the
# LOWER-median clamp, the same total tie order) with ONE input changed — a waiter's cost s
# is the tokens predicted resident in NEITHER the engine's GPU index NOR its CPU-tier
# shadow, so a block that is still restorable from the tier counts as CACHED. A returner
# whose CPU copy is alive therefore costs ~its new turn's tokens and is re-seated before it
# falls off the tier's cliff (measured: restored share 90 % under 1 min, 30 % at 1-3 min,
# 14 % at 3-5 min — and the scheduler's own entry wait for a seat-loss return is 328-420 s,
# i.e. the queue is what pushes returners over the cliff). A COLD returner keeps
# min(full, median), so it ages and overtakes; newcomers are untouched.
#
# THE TIER ADDS NO SEATS. These two values only SIZE the shadow (a model of vLLM's tier);
# the seat budget, the cold-entry valve and placement keep the GPU-only cost. Admission is
# never discounted by a restorable block (TestHrrnTierDoesNotDiscountTheSeatBudget).
#
# DEPLOYMENT FACTS (not knobs — they must describe the engine the pods actually run):
#   CPU_TIER_BYTES  = vLLM's --kv-transfer-config cpu_bytes_to_use (exp-ops DECODE_TIER_BYTES)
#   KV_BLOCK_BYTES  = 2 x layers x kv_heads x head_dim x dtype_bytes x VLLM_BLOCK_SIZE
#                     Qwen3-30B-A3B @ TP4, fp16, 64-token blocks = 98,304 B/token x 64
#                     = 6,291,456 B/block
#                     => the shadow's capacity = 549755813888 / 6291456 = 87,381 blocks
#                        = 2.17x the 40,183-block GPU pool (the measured "2.2x the pool")
#   If OFFLOAD=0, leave BOTH at 0: with no tier the module degenerates to F5′ exactly
#   (TestHrrnTierNoTierEqualsF5P, byte for byte against the archive F5′ golden).
#
# SHADOW VALIDATION (the arm's own gate): every seated RETURN logs a SHADOW-VALIDATION
# event (pred=<fraction> measured=<cached/prompt> fairness_id=<id>) and lands in
# llm_d_epp_group_tier_shadow_pairs_total{engine,pred_bin,meas_bin} — the AUC is computed
# from that 11x11 matrix (frozen: shadow AUC >= 0.8). llm_d_epp_group_tier_shadow_blocks
# and _capacity_blocks are the model's own fill.
#
# PRECONDITION, NOT YET DONE: the exp-ops emitter must render the two new keys
# (`cpuTierBytes`, `kvBlockBytes`) in the group-scheduler parameters block — docs/gsch-core/
# README.md §4e carries the patch. Until it does, this file's CPU_TIER_BYTES/KV_BLOCK_BYTES
# would be env values no template reads (the EPP would run the tier-less default and the
# arm would be F5′ under another name).
#
# The core is per-engine ONLY (no ENGINE_GROUPS knob), pins placement with its OWN Filter,
# and answers the flow-control gate with its OWN detector. See docs/gsch-core/README.md for
# the full chain audit.

EPP_IMAGE_TAG=groupsched-99a47617
EPP_IMAGE_DIGEST=sha256:1163763c0afbe97e116bbe29d71a830105c4c73c16f7811304920d769aac3c4b
EPP_IMAGE_DIGEST_AMD64=sha256:6207d362256d1708cc7f97673fb81d1c83f0449dea4023d3508eac62844522ca
REQUIRE_BUILD_PIN=1
CHAIN=groupsched-core
PROTOCOL_CELL=weka-c128
CONCURRENCY=128

# ---- the engine's CPU KV tier (the offload deployment) ----
OFFLOAD=1
DECODE_TIER_BYTES=549755813888

# ---- the core's parameters (base block: the same for every core arm) ----
GROUP_BUDGET_FRACTION=0.95
CORE_QUANTUM=4
IDLE_SECONDS=20
TTL_SECONDS=30
INFLIGHT_CAP=64
BLOCK_SIZE_TOKENS=64
CAPACITY_LIVENESS_SECONDS=120
INFLIGHT_REAP_SECONDS=3700
# the tier shadow's two facts (see the header). 0/0 = no tier = hrrn-tier ≡ F5′.
CPU_TIER_BYTES=549755813888
KV_BLOCK_BYTES=6291456

# ---- the module selectors (one value each; ONE differs from core-f5p-q4-offload.env) ----
CORE_SIZING=index
CORE_ENTRY_ORDER=hrrn-tier
CORE_ENGINE_CHOICE=most-free-budget
CORE_ROTATION=quantum
CORE_VICTIM=valve
CORE_SAFETY=none

# ---- the chain (see the audit) ----
BRANCH_PLUGIN=1
# YAML bool, VERBATIM into the plugin block: logRequests is a Go bool and the decode is
# strict, so `1` renders `logRequests: 1` (a number) and CrashLoops every arm.
BRANCH_LOG_REQUESTS=true
AFFINITY_FILTER=0
CORE_DETECTOR=group
BENCH_IMAGE=quay.io/dasari_surya_sai_venkatesh1/llm-d-benchmark:aiperf-rootid
